#: ../../desktop/usage.rst:3
msgid "Using the Client"
msgstr ""

#: ../../desktop/usage.rst:5
msgid "The Nextcloud desktop client runs in the background. Open its settings from the system tray on Windows and Linux or the menu bar on macOS."
msgstr ""

#: ../../desktop/usage.rst:11
msgid "Add account"
msgstr ""

#: ../../desktop/usage.rst:13
msgid "To connect another Nextcloud account, open the settings dialog and click **Add account** in the sidebar. Enter the address you use to access your Nextcloud server in a browser, then click **Log in**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../desktop/usage.rst:16
msgid "Setup wizard with the server address field and Log in button"
msgstr ""

#: ../../desktop/usage.rst:21
msgid "If your network requires a proxy, click **Proxy settings** before logging in. Choose the system proxy or enter your proxy settings manually, then click **Done**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../desktop/usage.rst:24
msgid "Proxy settings dialog with no proxy, system proxy, and manual proxy options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../desktop/usage.rst:29
msgid "If the secure connection fails, check the server address and contact your server administrator. The wizard may offer to connect without TLS or use a client certificate. Use **Use client certificate** only if your server requires one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../desktop/usage.rst:32
msgid "Warning that the secure server connection failed, with client certificate and unencrypted options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../desktop/usage.rst:37
msgid "If prompted for a client certificate, choose the PKCS#12 file provided by your administrator, enter its password, and click **Connect**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../desktop/usage.rst:40
msgid "Client certificate dialog with certificate file and password fields"
msgstr ""

#: ../../desktop/usage.rst:45
msgid "The wizard asks you to switch to your browser. Click **Open** if the browser does not open automatically. Log in and grant the desktop client access when prompted. Then return to the wizard."
msgstr ""

#: ../../desktop/usage.rst:48
msgid "Setup wizard prompting you to open a browser to authorize the account"
msgstr ""

#: ../../desktop/usage.rst:53
msgid "Choose how to sync your files. With classic synchronization, choose **Synchronize everything** or **Choose what to sync**. Use **Choose** beside **Local sync folder** to change where files are stored, then click **Done**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../desktop/usage.rst:56
msgid "Classic synchronization options and local sync folder in the setup wizard"
msgstr ""

#: ../../desktop/usage.rst:61
msgid "You can choose **File Provider** to download files on demand. Click **Done** to finish adding the account. On macOS, see :doc:`macosfileprovider` for details about Finder integration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../desktop/usage.rst:64
msgid "File Provider selected in the setup wizard"
msgstr ""

#: ../../desktop/usage.rst:69
msgid "Before finishing classic synchronization, click **Advanced** if you want confirmation before syncing large folders or external storage. Set your preferences in **Advanced options**, then click **Done** to return to the wizard."
msgstr ""

#: ../../desktop/usage.rst:72
msgid "Advanced options for large folders and external storage in the setup wizard"
msgstr ""

#: ../../desktop/usage.rst:78
msgid "Settings dialog"
msgstr ""

#: ../../desktop/usage.rst:80
msgid "Select an account in the sidebar to see its sync status, local folder, storage usage, and connection settings. Use **Add Folder Sync Connection** to set up another classic sync folder for that account. You can log out or remove the account from the same page."
msgstr ""

#: ../../desktop/usage.rst:84
msgid "Account settings with classic sync status, connection settings, and account controls"
msgstr ""

#: ../../desktop/usage.rst:89
msgid "Under **General**, choose whether to launch the client at startup, use monochrome icons, and show notifications. On macOS, you can also enable File Provider for all accounts. This setting replaces classic sync folders and their Finder integration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../desktop/usage.rst:93
msgid "General settings for startup, icons, File Provider, and notifications"
msgstr ""

#: ../../desktop/usage.rst:98
msgid "Under **Advanced**, set confirmation thresholds for large folders and external storage. You can also adjust the server polling interval, decide whether removed files go to the trash, edit ignored files, or create a debug archive."
msgstr ""

#: ../../desktop/usage.rst:101
msgid "Advanced settings for sync confirmations, server polling, ignored files, and debug archives"
msgstr ""

#: ../../desktop/usage.rst:108
msgid "To exclude files or folders from synchronization, click **Edit Ignored Files** under **Advanced**. Add a pattern for each item you want to ignore. An asterisk (``*``) matches any number of characters, a question mark (``?``) matches one character, and a trailing slash (``/``) limits a pattern to folders. Select **Allow Deletion** only for ignored items that the client may remove when they prevent a folder from being deleted. Click **OK** to save."
msgstr ""

#: ../../desktop/usage.rst:113
msgid "Ignored files editor with patterns, Allow Deletion checkboxes, and save controls"
msgstr ""

#: ../../desktop/usage.rst:118
msgid "Under **Info**, you can check the desktop client version and open its usage documentation or legal notice."
msgstr ""

#: ../../desktop/usage.rst:120
msgid "Info page showing the desktop client version and documentation link"
msgstr ""

#: ../../desktop/usage.rst:126
msgid "Systray icon"
msgstr ""

#: ../../desktop/usage.rst:128
msgid "The desktop client shows a status icon in the system tray on Windows and Linux or the menu bar on macOS. Colorful status icons and colorful or monochrome tray icons are available for the same sync states. You can choose monochrome icons under **General** in the settings dialog."
